# Media Workbench v2 — screen comp S1: Styles three-pane, Palette facet (conventional, macOS light appearance)
schema: "0.4"
id: mw-screen-styles
type: image
service: gemini
model: gemini-3.1-flash-image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    A straight-on screenshot of a macOS 14 Sonoma app window, light system appearance, SF Pro type, traffic lights, unified toolbar titled "Styles". The app is a media-generation workbench; this screen edits the layered house style that both instructs the image generator and grades its output.

    Far left: the translucent source-list sidebar: "Requests 3", "Library", "Runs 2", "Styles" (selected), divider, "Settings".

    Pane 1, "Layers": a vertical stack of four rows top to bottom joined by a thin line, each with a small toggle switch: "House" (caption "global"), "Project · codefre.sh" (caption "inherits House", a small dot showing unsaved), "Collection · landing" (caption "inherits Project"), "Prompt · pricing-hero". "Project" is selected.

    Pane 2, "Facets": a plain list: "Palette" (selected), "Typography", "Copy voice", "Element construction", "Imagery rules", "Rubric", "Snippets".

    Pane 3, the Palette editor (widest pane):
    - A row of five large colour swatches, each with a role label and hex below: "canvas #0F1115", "ink #F2F0EB", "accent #FF6B4A", "teal #2EC4B6", "muted #6B7280".
    - A compact table titled "Contrast pairs" with small sample text chips and ratios: "ink / canvas 16.6:1 AAA", "teal / canvas 8.7:1 AAA", "accent / canvas 6.7:1 AA", "muted / canvas 3.9:1 Large only" (orange), "ink / accent 2.5:1 Fail" (red).
    - Two rows of small flag chips: "Must use: accent" and "Avoid: purple gradient".
    - A quiet footer line: "Compiles to 3 rubric criteria".

    Native, tidy, left-aligned, one blue primary "Save" in the toolbar. Short legible labels and numbers only.
  negative: >
    garbled text, lorem ipsum, watermark, mobile frame, browser chrome, Windows UI,
    perspective tilt, synthesizer/audio-hardware look, CAD tool, manuscript editor,
    dark mode, colour wheel, gradient, Photoshop-style tool palette, emoji icons
  style: "UI design screen comp, straight-on screenshot framing, no perspective, no camera tilt, crisp pixel-sharp interface"
output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      quality: 95
  dimensions:
    width: 2560
    height: 1600
    aspect_ratio: "16:10"
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    depicts_the_product:
      weight: 0.4
      description: "reads as a media-generation request/review/grading tool, specifically editing a layered brand style (house to prompt) that feeds image generation and grading"
    follows_spec:
      weight: 0.35
      description: "shows (1) three panes: layer stack / facet list / facet editor; (2) a layer stack ordered House > Project > Collection > Prompt with enable toggles and inherits captions; (3) a palette editor with role-labelled swatches; (4) a contrast-pair table with WCAG ratios including at least one failing pair"
    macos_native:
      weight: 0.25
      description: "reads as a native macOS 14 light-appearance window with source list, split panes, SF type and system switches"
  reject_if:
    - depicts a different product category (paint app, CAD tool, manuscript editor, audio hardware, web page)
    - primary labels (Layers, Palette, contrast ratios) are unreadable or garbled
tags: [screen-comp, macos, media-workbench, v2]
